+    "safeguard.confirmation": "This is not a GBV case, not an unaccompanied or separated child, and not an immediate risk to life",
+    "safeguard.consequence": "If you cannot tick this, close the form and use the specialised pathway.",
+    "safeguard.referralExclusion": "<b>Three kinds of case do not belong on this form. Stop and use the proper pathway.</b> <ul> <li><b>Gender-based violence.</b> GBV cases follow the specialised, survivor-centred pathway of the protection cluster, with its own consent and its own confidential system. Never record a GBV referral in a shared coordination form, not even coded.</li> <li><b>An unaccompanied or separated child.</b> These go to child-protection case management. Around 200 were reported in one area alone on 14 September; each one is a case file, not a row.</li> <li><b>Immediate risk to life.</b> Act first. Record afterwards, if at all.</li> </ul> Recording these here would put people at risk and would break the consent under which they spoke to you. The count of such referrals can be reported to coordination as a number, by the pathway that holds them — never as records here.",
+    "svc.p001": "Service contact record — MHPSS Nepal",
+    "svc.p002": "Revised draft for field piloting <span>· saved on this phone, sent to the coordination register when there is signal</span>",
+    "svc.p003": "Service contact record",
+    "svc.p004": "Layer 1 · Rasuwa / Bhote Koshi",
+    "svc.p005": "← Forms",
+    "svc.p006": "Hub",
+    "svc.p007": "One contact with one person",
+    "svc.p008": "Use this when you have seen, spoken to or supported a specific person. For a group activity or a day's total, use the <a href=\"5ws-report.html\">activity report</a> instead — this form is deliberately one record per person per contact, because that is the only way a returning person can be recognised instead of counted twice.",
+    "svc.p009": "<b>The person's name and phone number stay on this handset.</b> You type a few details so the phone can work out a <b>contact code</b>; the details are used for that calculation and then discarded. Only the code is saved. Nobody downstream — not the coordination view, not the dashboard, not this site — ever receives the name, the number, or a date of birth.",
+    "svc.p010": "<b>Works with no signal.</b> Records are held on this phone as you save them and sent to the coordination register on their own when there is signal. The export remains for a copy of your own. <span id=\"storeWarn\"></span>",
