+    "svc.p012": "remembered for next time",
+    "svc.p013": "Reporting organisation",
+    "svc.p014": "Name of organisation",
+    "svc.p015": "Focal point name",
+    "svc.p016": "A staff member, never a service user.",
+    "svc.p017": "Focal point phone",
+    "svc.p018": "Type of service provider",
+    "svc.p019": "Who actually delivered this contact. Asked for on 15 September so that counsellors, psychologists and psychiatrists can be counted apart.",
+    "svc.p020": "When and where",
+    "svc.p021": "Date — Gregorian (AD)",
+    "svc.p022": "This is the date the system sorts and groups on.",
+    "svc.p023": "Date — Bikram Sambat <span class=\"opt\">— optional</span>",
+    "svc.p024": "Typed as reported. <b>Not converted automatically</b> — that needs a verified BS calendar table, which has not been obtained.",
+    "svc.p025": "District",
+    "svc.p026": "Site",
+    "svc.p027": "From the holding-centre roster. Only choose “Other” if the site genuinely is not listed — every “Other” has to be reconciled by hand later.",
+    "svc.p028": "Municipality and ward <span class=\"opt\">— optional</span>",
+    "svc.p029": "Asked for on 15 September as province / subdistrict. Free text for now: the agreed municipality and ward code list has not been obtained.",
+    "svc.p030": "Name of site",
+    "svc.p031": "Location pin <span class=\"opt\">— optional</span>",
+    "svc.p032": "📍 Use my location",
+    "svc.p033": "Recorded to three decimal places — a grid of roughly 100 m. Enough to put the site on a map; not enough to point at a household. A precise pin, a small count and a target group together identify people even with no name attached, which is why the precision is reduced here rather than in the dashboard.",
+    "svc.p034": "The person",
+    "svc.p035": "Is this the first time your organisation has recorded this person?",
+    "svc.p036": "New — first contact",
+    "svc.p037": "Returning — seen before",
+    "svc.p038": "Not known",
+    "svc.p039": "This is the question that makes the cumulative figure mean something. On 15 September the reported total was over 9,000 with duplication nobody could size.",
+    "svc.p040": "<b>These four boxes are not saved.</b> They are read, combined into a code, and cleared when you save. Type them the same way each time and the same person gets the same code.",
+    "svc.p041": "Initials",
+    "svc.p042": "First letters of the name, as the person says it.",
+    "svc.p043": "Year of birth",
+    "svc.p044": "Year only — never a full date.",
+    "svc.p045": "Sex",
+    "svc.p046": "— choose —",
+    "svc.p047": "Female",
+    "svc.p048": "Male",
+    "svc.p049": "Other",
+    "svc.p050": "Not stated",
+    "svc.p051": "Municipality",
+    "svc.p052": "Where the person is from, not where you met them.",
+    "svc.p053": "Contact code",
+    "svc.p054": "— fill the four boxes above —",
+    "svc.p055": "This is the only part that is saved. It is a <b>pseudonym, not an anonymous token</b>: the four inputs vary little, so someone holding a list of candidate names could test them against a code. Adequate for agreeing these questions; a live register needs the code mixed with a secret this handset never holds, which means a server.",
